<!--
  Status-bar icon: shuttlecock, cork plus a SOLID skirt (the "Shuttle" mark),
  tilted 26 degrees to match tools/make_icons.py's TILT. Android alpha-masks
  small icons, so this is a monochrome shape on transparent ground and NOT
  @mipmap/ic_launcher — see CLAUDE.md. The two apps must never share a
  silhouette; telling them apart at a glance is the point of having them.

  Both choices were made by rendering at 18px (tools/preview_notif_icons.py).
  Stroked feathers went wispy and read as a trident, hence solid mass. And 26
  is ~5 degrees past this cone's own 20.8 flare, so the trailing edge sits past
  vertical and it reads more wedge than shuttlecock — the accepted price of
  matching the launcher (Samyak, 2026-08-01; 12 was the largest lean that still
  stood up, if this ever wants revisiting). Coordinates are baked rather than
  wrapped in a <group android:rotation>, so what ships is what was previewed.
-->
